cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite this repository as preliminary research software. The dataset is an
  unreviewed draft and the smoke results are not validated benchmark findings.
type: software
title: 'Bangla-Cal: Bengali calibration and hallucination benchmark toolkit'
authors:
  - family-names: Bhuiyan
    given-names: Niloy
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Niloy-Bhuiyan/bangla-cal'
url: 'https://github.com/Niloy-Bhuiyan/bangla-cal'
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Python toolkit for evaluating confidence calibration,
  hallucination, and abstention in Bengali question answering using free-tier
  Gemini, free-tier Groq, and local Ollama. Includes draft question data,
  question-level bootstrap intervals, independent judge/human validation
  workflows, and explicitly preliminary real-model smoke artifacts.
keywords:
  - Bengali
  - calibration
  - hallucination
  - evaluation
